section: compiler
synopsis: The pattern-match checker no longer assumes that pattern synonym matches force their argument
description:
  A match on a pattern synonym excludes ⊥ as a value of the scrutinee only
  through a ``COMPLETE`` set: when every member that can match at the type of
  the scrutinee failed to match, and that type has a value other than ⊥.
  Hence ``-Wredundant-bang-patterns`` and ``-Woverlapping-patterns`` no longer
  report bangs or clauses as redundant or inaccessible when deleting them
  would change the semantics, and ``-Wincomplete-patterns`` reports matches
  that fail on ⊥ fields that a pattern synonym does not force. Redundancy that
  rests on the strictness of a pattern synonym outside of an exhausted
  ``COMPLETE`` set is no longer reported.
